WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:10.967
Dr. Maya (Lead Instructor): Welcome. Today we explore Plate Tectonics & Boundary Dynamics — moving beyond textbook definitions to discover how nature actually behaves in the real physical universe.

2
00:10.967 --> 00:25.233
Dr. Maya (Lead Instructor): Observe this real-world event: Subducting Pacific slab releasing volatiles into the mantle wedge, lowering melting point and producing volcanic eruptions.. This isn't an abstract equation; it is governing the real world right now.

3
00:25.233 --> 00:40.733
Dr. Maya (Lead Instructor): The underlying mathematical law is formulated as: \sigma_{lith} = E \cdot \epsilon + \eta \cdot \dot{\epsilon} \quad \text{(Viscoelastic Slab Pull & Ridge Push)}. Notice how each variable directly maps to a physical property of the system.

4
00:40.733 --> 00:49.200
Alex (Curious Student): Isn't it true that Tectonic plates float like boats on top of a completely liquid ocean of molten magma.?

5
00:49.200 --> 01:07.600
Dr. Maya (Lead Instructor): That is a very common intuitive pitfall! But in reality: The asthenosphere is over 98% solid crystalline rock that creeps via plastic viscoelastic deformation under high pressure and temperature.. True molten liquid magma only exists in isolated melt pockets and volcanic magma chambers.

6
01:07.600 --> 01:18.967
Dr. Maya (Lead Instructor): Now that you've mastered the fundamentals of Plate Tectonics & Boundary Dynamics, it is time to test your intuition in the interactive revision sandbox. Let's begin!
